{"data":{"repository":{"pullRequest":{"headRefOid":"0b4979114fa2e9c00bb30285ceab79f171209913","baseRefOid":"95fe6b3c5e7414743c3095624a0821b895373d6f","reviewThreads":{"nodes":[{"id":"PRRT_kwDOUMS7-s6xzsn7","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"viewerCanResolve":true,"viewerCanUnresolve":false,"path":"src/services/github/stacks.ts","line":210,"originalLine":210,"startLine":205,"diffSide":"RIGHT","comments":{"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOUMS7-s8AAAABB2qFKQ","databaseId":4419388713,"author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve the pending merge request returned with HTTP 409**\n\nIf a user retries after an `unknown` outcome while GitHub is still processing the merge, the PUT returns HTTP 409 with the existing request's UUID and merge options. The `ghGlobal` wrapper rejects nonzero exits, so this catch turns that response into a merge failure and discards the UUID, even though the stack may still merge. Handle this response separately and report the pending request or poll it after verifying its options. The [async merge documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/pulls/pulls?apiVersion=2026-03-10#merge-a-pull-request-asynchronously) explicitly describes 409 as an existing pending merge request, not a failed merge.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->","createdAt":"2026-10-30T00:46:17Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-30T00:46:17Z","url":"https://github.com/JonathanRReed/Good-GH-CLI/pull/17#discussion_r4419388713","outdated":false}],"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpK0MjAyNi0xMC0zMFQwMDo0NjoxN1rPAAAAAQdqhSk="}}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOUMS7-s6xzsn8","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"viewerCanResolve":true,"viewerCanUnresolve":false,"path":"src/services/github/stacks.ts","line":227,"originalLine":227,"startLine":226,"diffSide":"RIGHT","comments":{"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOUMS7-s8AAAABB2qFKg","databaseId":4419388714,"author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Invalidate cached PR lists after stacked merge attempts**\n\nWhen a user has populated the PR-list cache before merging a native stack, this path never invalidates it. `listPullRequests` caches results for 120 seconds, so subsequent listings can continue showing every merged stack member as open until the cache expires. The existing `mergePullRequest` implementation invalidates `pr-list:` in a `finally` block; apply the same invalidation here, including unknown outcomes where the server may have completed the merge.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->","createdAt":"2026-10-30T00:46:17Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-30T00:46:17Z","url":"https://github.com/JonathanRReed/Good-GH-CLI/pull/17#discussion_r4419388714","outdated":false}],"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpK0MjAyNi0xMC0zMFQwMDo0NjoxN1rPAAAAAQdqhSo="}}}],"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpK0MjAyNi0xMC0zMFQwMDo0NjoxN1rOsc7J_A=="}}}}}}